/* ==========================================================================
   ICA Usage Tracker — Daily Data File
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   HOW TO UPDATE (every day at 6 PM):
     1. Open your Excel tracker.
     2. Find today's date column and note who used which assistants.
     3. Edit the LATEST entry at the top of TRACKER_DATA below:
          - Change "dateKey"     → today's date as "YYYY-MM-DD"
          - Change "sourceColumn"→ the column header label from your Excel
            (e.g. "Wed-22-Jul-26")
          - Update each person's "assistants" array ONLY — no other fields needed:
              • List the assistant name(s) they used  → used = true  (auto-derived)
              • Empty array []                        → not used     (auto-derived)
              • ["On Leave"]                          → on leave     (auto-derived)
     4. In index.html, find the tracker-data.js <script> tag and update the
        ?v= query param to match the new dateKey (e.g. ?v=2026-07-23).
        This busts the browser cache so everyone sees the fresh data immediately.
     5. Save both files and git commit + push.
        Everyone on GitHub Pages instantly sees the new data — no server needed.

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   DATA FORMAT:
     TRACKER_DATA is an object keyed by "YYYY-MM-DD".
     Each value has:
       dateKey      — same as the key, e.g. "2026-07-22"
       sourceColumn — the Excel column header, e.g. "Wed-22-Jul-26"
       uploadedAt   — ISO timestamp of when you last edited this entry
       records      — array of { email, name, team, fte, assistants }
                      (used & onLeave are derived automatically from assistants)
   ========================================================================== */

